<article class="env-remark" id="A863E1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/A863E1">Remark <span data-tag="A863E1">2.2.5.5</span>.</a> Since every inner anodyne map is a categorical equivalence, it follows that every categorical fibration $p: X \rightarrow S$ is a inner fibration (see Definition <a href="/tag/04D6DB" data-tag="04D6DB">2.0.0.3</a>). The converse is false in general; however, it is true when $S$ is a point. In other words, the fibrant objects for the Joyal model structure on $\sSet $ are precisely the $\infty $-categories. The proof will be given in §<a href="/tag/D26ECA" data-tag="D26ECA">2.4.6</a>, as Theorem <a href="/tag/945046" data-tag="945046">2.4.6.1</a>. We will assume this result for the remainder of the section. No circularity will result from this, since the proof of Theorem <a href="/tag/945046" data-tag="945046">2.4.6.1</a> will not use any of the results proven below. </p>
</article>